  "description": "In-house glob matcher, matched against a whole logical path without a leading /, or against a file name. Braces are expanded first, into at most 1024 patterns; the pattern matches when one of its expansions matches. A character is a Unicode scalar value encoded in valid UTF-8; each byte that is not part of a valid UTF-8 sequence counts as one character, which only ?, * and negated classes match. Characters are compared exactly: NFC and case folding (§11.3) belong to the rule matcher.",
